  "thought": "If the nearest available customer is farther than twice the average distance of customers from the depot, the truck waits at its current position; otherwise, it heads to the nearest customer. This heuristic avoids long deadhead trips when customers are clustered near the depot, anticipating that future customers may appear closer."
